{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum loss of each lottery, prioritizing losses over gains and preferring the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., less severe) maximum loss. In this decision problem, both Lottery A and Lottery B have a minimum outcome of 0 Euros. Therefore, the maximum loss for both lotteries is 0 Euros. Since there are no actual losses (negative outcomes) in either lottery, the maximum loss is identical (neutral) for both. Thus, the decision reason would be indifferent between the two lotteries because neither involves a loss. The relevant information — the worst possible outcome of each lottery — is available and identical in both cases.",
